WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:00.900
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
This week, we're

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.420
talking all about machine
learning-- the hardware, making

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.910
recommendations, and how
TensorFlow Enterprise could

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.178
optimize your business.

00:00:07.178 --> 00:00:09.720
I'm Mark, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.108
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:12.108 --> 00:00:14.400
Google Cloud offers a range
of solutions for enterprise

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.200
situations, allowing
customers to choose

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.810
what fits best for them,
even down to the chip.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.810
Recently, Google Cloud TPUs
broke the scalability records

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.120
for inference, adding to
the previous record-breaking

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.450
success for learning.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.660
So if cutting edge
deep learning workloads

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.310
are a core part of
our business, you'll

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.045
want to take a
look at Cloud TPUs.

00:00:32.045 --> 00:00:33.420
It's nothing
unusual to recommend

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.850
ways to optimize your cloud
infrastructure and security

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:36.730
settings.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.090
But what is unusual is how
Google Cloud uses machine

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.290
learning to power
our suggestions.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.070
One such tool is the Cloud
Identity and Access Management

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.713
Recommender, which
we've cracked open

00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:47.880
for a behind the scenes
look at the machine learning

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.590
that powers it.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.840
TensorFlow is one of the
most popular machine learning

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.490
frameworks, which
was made universally

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.890
useful with the launch
of TensorFlow Enterprise.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.320
And now, we're expanding on
the enterprise-grade support

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.695
and performance
with improvements

00:00:59.695 --> 00:01:02.250
in reading data from Cloud
Storage and BigQuery.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.769
The speed of getting data from
Storage to the ML training

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:07.600
process can be critical
for AI-enabled businesses,

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.760
so we're here to optimize.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.350
KubeCon and CloudNativeCon
2019 is happening right now,

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.478
November 18 through 21,
in San Diego, California.

00:01:16.478 --> 00:01:19.020
If you want to learn more about
Cloud solutions of all sorts,

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:19.890
you should come.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.967
Registration is still open,
and it'll be available on site.

00:01:22.967 --> 00:01:25.050
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.130
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.270
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.980
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.480
We'll see you in the cloud.

